YAAD: What more could I have done? (Long post)

I had a pretty good Valkyrie going, found a BoH in Sokoban, cleared
out the mines and started making my way deeper into the dungeon. I had
lost a couple of characters earlier to a random wand-of-death-carrying
monster out in the dungeon, so I was getting a little concerned around
DLvl 20 because I still had no reflection.

So far I had found 2 un-identified amulets. I ID'd them and they
turned out to be strangulation and restful sleep (i.e. no good to me
right now). I had cleared out everything very carefully not exposing
myself to long direct corridors in case of WoD.

I usually don't like to go below Medusa without having a pretty good
set of equipment becuase I find it tedious to keep levitating or
water-walking back and forth across the island trying to find stuff.
But this time, I had no choice. I went across, killed Medusa, went
down and found the castle. I thought that maybe I could sneak in the
back and get the dragons - just my luck 3 black dragons and a green
dragon. I wasn't sure then if BDSM protected against wands of death (I
know now that they do not), so I retreated.

On the same level as my base camp, I found a vault with the portal to
Fort Ludios. Everytime I have found Ludios (which isn't many) and gone
in, I have seen at least 1 soldier with a wand of death, so even
though there was a silver dragon hanging out in there, I didn't want
to risk it.

What to do? What to do? I decided to make the most of my wands of
polymorph (I had two). I poly'd the two amulets and got 2 more un-ID'd
amulets. One turned out to be ESP, the other turned out to be changing
which I found out the hard way since I didn't have any scrolls of ID.
I put it on and it turned to dust (great). I poly'd my one remaining
amulet and got a new, previously unseen one. I thought that maybe it
was life saving or reflection. A zap of cold against the wall proved
it not to be reflection, so I kept it just in case it was life saving
(which it wasn't - turned out to be magical breathing, but I didn't
find out until I ran out of polymorph charges).

So I figured that was a bust, maybe I can get lucky and poly for a
shield of reflection. Gathered up all of the Elven and magical stuff
that I had and didn't need. Poly'd several times with no luck. Got
another cloak of displacement and boots of levitation and maybe even
water walking, but still no reflection.

Oh - I know! My magic lamp! I blessed it and rubbed it. Guess what?
That's right - hostile djinni. How about each and every fountain I've
seen along the way - no luck - no wishes.

Finally I said screw it, let's give Ludios a try. I went in and as I
was fighting off the first wave of soldiers I see a black ray go by
me. He had aimed at my displaced image. I figured that was about as
good as my luck was going to get so I got out of Dodge.

How about the castle - surely there can't be someone with a wand of
death in both places, right? I went in, opened the drawbridge and
retreated to a good location to fight one at a time. Cleared out the
first wave of monsters including two liches without too much
excitement. All that was left was a peaceful Tengu and an Olog-hai.
The Tengu kept getting in the way and the Olog-hai wouldn't enter the
corridor to come face me. So I got tired of waiting, and decided to go
get him. I took two steps toward him in the corridor. DYWYPI? Kory -
killed by a death ray.

To add insult to injury, about 1000 turns before all of this, I was
waiting long periods of time in the maze level just above the castle
and a silver dragon appeared. I dispatched him, and yep - no scales
left behind, but I had two sets of black, a set of green, and a set of
orange.

Three questions:
a) what else could I have done?
b) is there anything in the code that prevents wands of death before a
certain dungeon level? I never usually see one that high, but they get
more common the lower I go.
c) I know that dragons won't breathe on me at distance of 1, but that
Olog-hai would have zapped me, right?

